{"name":"Cube Farm","hex":"#b2b6be","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cube farm","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large group of cubicles, or a building, campus, or area abundant in them."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cube_farm"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cubicle","blocks":[{"text":"A cubicle is an enclosed office that is separated from neighboring workspaces, with partitions that are usually 5–6 feet (1.5–1.8 m) tall. Its purpose is to isolate office workers and managers from the sights and noises of an open workspace so that they may concentrate with fewer distractions. Cubicles are composed of modular elements such as walls, work surfaces, overhead bins, drawers, and shelving, which can be configured depending on the user's needs. Installation is generally performed by trained personnel, although some cubicles allow configuration changes to be performed by users without specific training."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/CubeSpace.jpg/330px-CubeSpace.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cubicle"},{"title":"Cube","blocks":[{"text":"A cube is a three-dimensional solid object in geometry. It has eight vertices and twelve straight edges of the same length, so that these edges form six square faces of the same size. It is an example of a polyhedron. It is a special case of a cuboid, a parallelepiped, and a rhombohedron in which all six quadrilateral faces are squares. It is a three-dimensional hypercube, a family of polytopes that also includes the two-dimensional square and four-dimensional tesseract."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Cube-h.svg/330px-Cube-h.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cube"},{"title":"Farm","blocks":[{"text":"A farm is an area of land that is devoted primarily to agricultural processes with the primary objective of producing food and other crops; it is the basic facility in food production. The name is used for specialized units such as arable farms, vegetable farms, fruit farms, dairy, pig and poultry farms, and land used for the production of natural fiber, biofuel, and other biobased products. It includes ranches, feedlots, orchards, plantations and estates, smallholdings, and hobby farms, and includes the farmhouse and agricultural buildings as well as the land. In modern times, the term has been extended to include such industrial operations as wind farms and fish farms, both of which can operate on land or at sea."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Church_Farm%2C_Stockton%2C_Norfolk_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1968544.jpg/330px-Church_Farm%2C_Stockton%2C_Norfolk_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1968544.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farm"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Cubicles.shop.jpg/500px-Cubicles.shop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Cubicles.shop.jpg/1280px-Cubicles.shop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Cubicles.shop.jpg/500px-Cubicles.shop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"3D model of cubicles","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACubicles.shop.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Digital_carrel_classroom.webp/500px-Digital_carrel_classroom.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Digital_carrel_classroom.webp/1280px-Digital_carrel_classroom.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Digital_carrel_classroom.webp/500px-Digital_carrel_classroom.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"3D model of cubicles in the classroom to get power to the desk and computers in the classroom for a computational education","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADigital_carrel_classroom.webp"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Cubicle-in-urban-high-rise.jpg/500px-Cubicle-in-urban-high-rise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Cubicle-in-urban-high-rise.jpg/1280px-Cubicle-in-urban-high-rise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Cubicle-in-urban-high-rise.jpg/500px-Cubicle-in-urban-high-rise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A cubicle in an urban high rise setting","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACubicle-in-urban-high-rise.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Photograph_of_the_Division_of_Classification_and_Cataloging%2C_1937.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Photograph_of_the_Division_of_Classification_and_Cataloging%2C_1937.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Photograph_of_the_Division_of_Classification_and_Cataloging%2C_1937.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Photograph_of_the_Division_of_Classification_and_Cataloging%2C_1937.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Photograph_of_the_Division_of_Classification_and_Cataloging%2C_1937.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Photograph_of_the_Division_of_Classification_and_Cataloging%